.TH geectl-remote-unlock 1  "geectl-remote-unlock 0.3.0" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-unlock \- Unlock a project or a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the unlock. The message is required: the server refuses an unlock without a comment
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote unlock\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-comment\fR> <\fIPROJECT\fR> [\fIPACKAGE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Unlock a project or a package. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the unlock. The message is required: the server refuses an unlock without a comment
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR \fI<COMMENT>\fR
A message recorded on the unlock
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project to unlock
.TP
[\fIPACKAGE\fR]
The package to unlock. Omit to unlock the whole project
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
